              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4800' id='1135' type-v2='text' w='53200' x='46267' y='13600'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='6'>Vendor Count</run>
                  <run fontsize='6'> and </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontsize='6'>Main Cuisines Count</run>
                  <run fontsize='6'>&apos;s color coding is based on the percentage of the Country&apos;s Maximum Vendor Count. </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontsize='6'>For example, if the hexagon with most vendor&apos;s in the country has 1000, then a hexagon with 1000  will have the </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#108040' fontsize='6'>darkest green</run>
                  <run fontsize='6'>, a hexagon with 500 will have</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#f1ce63' fontsize='6'>Æ </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#f1ce63' fontsize='6'>yellow</run>
                  <run fontsize='6'> and a hexagon with 0 will have the </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#fc0107' fontsize='6'>darkest red</run>
                  <run fontsize='6'>.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                </formatted-text>
